# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF in the working copy, which
# makes a fresh clone differ byte-for-byte from the checkout it was cloned from.
# `tools/doctor.mjs` compares the installed plugin copy against the source
# checkout and would then report a spurious difference, and `npm pack` would ship
# CRLF into `.mjs` files. Both are avoidable.
#
# `.ps1` files are also forced to LF: PowerShell reads either ending, and a
# consistent ending keeps the byte comparison meaningful.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets keep their bytes untouched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.gguf binary

# Git manages these itself.
*.zstd binary
